d prosperity  and stability in the pacific are upheld  and strengthened  a priority the white house says despite  the war and pandemic that have consumed  much of his presidency john hendren al  jazeera  let's get more on the visit from al  jazeera's florence louis who's in seoul  what message is the u.s intending to  send  with this visit florence  well south korea and japan are already  key allies of the us but the us says it  wants to strengthen those ties even  further and we're likely to see that  take the form of perhaps new trade and  business and technology deals perhaps an  upgrading of existing security  partnerships now it's also important to  note that just a week ago president  biden hosted southeast asian leaders in  the u.s and at that summit analysts say  it wasn't part of an effort to prevent  china from dominating the indo-pacific  region so this trip really is to rally  its  allies in east asia to send a message to  its friends and allies and also a  message to china that the u.s is back  it's committed to the region and it  wants the indo-pacific to remain free  and open and this is a message that  we've heard the biden administration  make time and again  now for countries in this region however  china remains a very important partner  especially in trade so for them it's not  going to be a matter of having to choose  which country they want to align  themselves to but more of  committed but more of conducting a fine  balancing act between these two powerful  nations and what specifically is the  president hoping to achieve there in  south korea  well denuclearization of north korea is  going to be high on the agenda  especially given reports that north  korea could be conducting a seventh  nuclear test but trade and technology is  also very important for both the us and  also south korea um we've seen the world  um go through a shortage of computer  chips and that's had an effect on the  availability of vehicles of kitchen  appliances and other goods that supply  chain crunch has had an effect has  contributed rather to inflation and the  us is keen to prevent those problems  come going forward so one way to do that  is to have those chips manufactured in  the u.s and at the moment the u.s only  produces about 10 percent of computer  chips so the plant  and it's significant that president  biden his first trip or his first visit  rather in south korea is going to be a  visit to a samsung chip manufacturing  plant and that plant is going to serve  as a model for a plant that samsung is  building in the u.s now president biden  is also expected to make a case for a  bill that he once passed that will see  the u.s bolster chip production and also  help protect it from future supply chain  problems in asia now it's not just a win  for u.s it's also a win for south korea  it's already an important player in the  chip industry but obviously it wants a  bigger market share and its tie-ups with  the u.s will help it do that because  more plants means more outputs and  greater market share  florence many thanks indeed al jazeera's  flores louis there live in seoul
 

